g and"},{"surface":"ஆடுகம்","parts":[{"text":"ஆடுகம்","lemma":"ஆடுதல்","gloss":"let us play"}],"gloss":"let us play"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செல்வல்","parts":[{"text":"செல்வல்","lemma":"செல்லுதல்","gloss":"I will go"}],"gloss":"I will go"},{"surface":"அத்தை","parts":[{"text":"அத்தை","lemma":"அத்தை","gloss":"expletive particle"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"யானே","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"யான்","gloss":"I"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"I indeed"},{"surface":"செல்லாது","parts":[{"text":"செல்லாது","lemma":"செல்லுதல்","gloss":"remaining"}],"gloss":"remaining"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மழை","parts":[{"text":"மழை","lemma":"மழை","gloss":"cloud"}],"gloss":"cloud"},{"surface":"அண்ணாப்ப","parts":[{"text":"அண்ணாப்ப","lemma":"அண்ணாத்தல்","gloss":"reaching up to"}],"gloss":"reaching up to"},{"surface":"நீடிய","parts":[{"text":"நீடிய","lemma":"நீடுதல்","gloss":"extended"}],"gloss":"extended"},{"surface":"நெடு","parts":[{"text":"நெடு","lemma":"நெடுமை","gloss":"tall"}],"gloss":"tall"},{"surface":"வரை","parts":[{"text":"வரை","lemma":"வரை","gloss":"mountain"}],"gloss":"mountain"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கழை","parts":[{"text":"கழை","lemma":"கழை","gloss":"bamboo"}],"gloss":"bamboo"},{"surface":"வளர்","parts":[{"text":"வளர்","lemma":"வளர்தல்","gloss":"growing"}],"gloss":"growing"},{"surface":"இமயம்","parts":[{"text":"இமயம்","lemma":"இமயம்","gloss":"Himalayas"}],"gloss":"Himalayas"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"போல","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நிலீஇயர்","parts":[{"text":"நிலீஇயர்","lemma":"நிலைபெறுதல்","gloss":"may you endure"}],"gloss":"may you endure"},{"surface":"அத்தை","parts":[{"text":"அத்தை","lemma":"அத்தை","gloss":"expletive particle"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"நிலம்","parts":[{"text":"நிலம்","lemma":"நிலம்","gloss":"earth"}],"gloss":"earth"},{"surface":"மிசையானே","parts":[{"text":"மிசை","lemma":"மிசை","gloss":"upon"},{"text":"ஆன்","lemma":"ஆன்","gloss":"locative suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"upon indeed"}]}],"literal":"Well-examined long erect matted hair / of the ancient first lord, without leaving his mouth, / having cherished the one, of the two times two / six-understood unique ancient treatise, / those who saw debate, to subdue their pride, / understanding falsehood that is like truth, / rejecting falsehood and establishing truth, / having completed without obstacle the twenty-one paths, / O descendant of wise people of praise-worthy excellence! / Requiring for the ritual, worn by you, / the skin of the buck of the forest deer, / shining upon the thread worn on the shoulder, / of rare virtue that shunned evil, / wearing bangles praised by righteousness, / small forehead, large wide hips, / few words, abundant hair, your / matching your status, your equal wives, / to obey the duties assigned to themselves, / whether forest or country, there / without omitting the fourteen places, / offering ghee so that water feels ashamed, / and sacrificing many so that calculation feels ashamed, / and spreading fame so that the earth feels ashamed, / at the great time of rare ritual, / your perfect eminent state of receiving guests, / may we always see indeed, ah! In the west, / if the thunderbolt of the cloud roars on the gold-producing tall mountain, / Kaveri nourishing with fresh water blooming with flowers, / there in our village of cool water gardens, / eating, chewing, riding, let us play. / I will go indeed, but without going, / like the bamboo-growing Himalayas, the tall mountain extended to reach up to the clouds, / may you endure indeed upon the earth!","translation":"O descendant of wise men of praise-worthy excellence! You follow the unique, ancient treatise of six parts (the Vedangas) that arose from the four Vedas cherished as one, which never leave the mouth of the ancient first Lord (Shiva) with long, erect matted hair. To subdue the pride of those who engage in hostile debates, you understand the falsehood that resembles truth, reject it, and establish the truth. You have completed without obstacle the twenty-one kinds of sacrifices. For the sacred rituals, you wear the skin of the forest buck, shining upon the sacred thread on your shoulder. Your wives, who match your status, have small foreheads, wide hips, speak few words, and have abundant hair; they obey the duties assigned to them. Whether in the forest or in the country, without omitting any of the fourteen places of sacrifice, you offer ghee so abundantly that water feels ashamed, perform so many sacrifices that numbers feel ashamed, and spread your fame so that the earth feels ashamed. May we always behold your perfect, eminent state of receiving guests at the great time of these rare rituals! In our village, situated where the Kaveri river, filled with fresh water and blooming flowers, nourishes the land when the thunder of clouds roars on the gold-bearing western mountains, we shall eat, drink, ride, and rejoice. I shall take my leave now; but may you, remaining here, endure upon this earth like the bamboo-growing Himalayas, the tall mountain that reaches up to the clouds!","modern":"நன்றாக ஆராயப்பட்ட, நீண்ட, நிமிர்ந்த சடையையுடைய பழமையான முதல்வனாகிய சிவபெருமானின் வாயிலிருந்து நீங்காது விளங்கும், ஒப்பற்றதாகப் போற்றப்படும் நான்கு வேதங்களின் ஆறு அங்கங்களையும் உணர்ந்த பழமையான நூலின்படி, வாதம் செய்வோரின் செருக்கை அடக்குவதற்காக, மெய் போன்ற பொய்களை ஆராய்ந்து அறிந்து, அப்பொய்களை நீக்கி மெய்ம்மையைக் கொண்டு, இருபத்தொரு வேள்வித் துறைகளையும் தடையின்றி முடித்த, புகழ்பெற்ற சிறப்பினை உடைய அறிஞர்களின் மரபில் வந்தவனே! வேள்வித் தொழிலுக்காக நீ அணிந்துள்ள காட்டில் வாழும் புல்வாய் என்னும் மானின் தோலானது, உனது தோளில் அணிந்துள்ள பூணூலின் மேல் விளங்குகின்றது. தீமைகளை நீக்கிய அரிய கற்பினையும், அறம் போற்றும் வளையல்களையும் அணிந்த, சிறிய நெற்றியும், பெரிய அகன்ற அல்குலும், சில சொற்களும், அடர்ந்த கூந்தலும் உடைய, உனது நிலைக்கு ஏற்ற உனது மனைவியர் தமக்குரிய கடமைகளைக் கேட்டுச் செய்ய, காடு என்றும் நாடு என்றும் கூறப்படும் பதினான்கு இடங்களிலும் தடையின்றி, நீர் நாணும்படி நெய்யை வாரி வழங்கியும், எண்கள் நாணும்படி பல வேள்விகளைச் செய்தும், நிலமகள் நாணும்படி உனது புகழைப் பரப்பியும், அரிய வேள்வி செய்யும் பெரிய காலங்களில் விருந்தினரை வரவேற்கும் உனது சிறந்த நிலையை நாங்களும் எப்போதும் காண்போமாக! மேற்கே பொன் விளையும் நீண்ட மலையில் மேகம் இடித்து முழங்கும்போது, மலர்கள் விரிந்த புதுநீரைக் கொண்டு காவிரியாறு பாயும் குளிர்ந்த நீர்நிலைகளையுடைய எமது ஊரின்கண் யாம் உண்டும் தின்றும் குதிரை முதலியவற்றில் ஊர்ந்தும் விளையாடுவோம். யான் இப்போது செல்வேன்; மேகங்கள் தொடுமாறு உயர்ந்து நீண்ட, மூங்கில்கள் வளரும் இமயமலை போல, நீ இந்நிலவுலகில் என்றும் நிலைபெற்று வாழ்வாயாக!","explanation":"The poet Avur Mulankilar addresses Kauniyan Vinnandayan, a learned Brahmin of Puncharrur in the Chola country. The poem belongs to the Vagai tinai and the theme of Parppana Vagai, which celebrates the victory and excellence of Brahmins in their spiritual and ritual duties. The poet praises Vinnandayan's mastery of the Vedas and Vedangas, his flawless performance of the twenty-one types of sacrifices, and his adherence to truth over false arguments. He describes the Brahmin's simple attire, wearing a deer skin over his sacred thread, and praises his virtuous wives who assist him in his rituals. The poet marvels at the scale of Vinnandayan's sacrifices, where ghee is poured so generously that water is put to shame, and so many rituals are performed that numbers themselves are baffled. Finally, the poet wishes him a long life as enduring as the Himalayas, while expressing his own desire to return to his fertile village nourished by the Kaveri river.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}